    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive alignment, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.29) and **Yordan Alvarez** (72.69). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serves as our premier target, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Bradley; his elite speed profile combined with a 14% platoon boost and a slow delivery from the opposing pitcher makes him an essential start for our stolen base needs. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a core anchor despite a left-on-left disadvantage, as his elite xwOBA of 0.475 and a top-order lineup placement provide a high floor that mitigates any negative platoon variance. **Junior Caminero** (66.95) and **Colt Keith** (69.64) also present strong value, with **Junior Caminero** benefiting from favorable wind conditions, though he and **Caleb Durbin** carry a slight risk due to a 39% rain probability in their respective contests.\n\nOur bench strategy was dominated by the decision regarding **Casey Schmitt** (47.68). While **Casey Schmitt** offered a solid platoon advantage and a projected spot in the three-hole, he fell just short of our daily efficiency threshold compared to the rest of the utility and middle infield options. Meanwhile, the optimizer continues to fade players like **Carson Benge** (35.79) and **Jacob Gonzalez** (35.58) as they fall well below our 40-point floor; their current projections struggle to overcome difficult matchups against pitchers like Luzardo and Williams. We remain cautious with **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith**, as both rely on pending lineups; however, the soft matchup against the 5.30 xERA of Rodriguez keeps them firmly in our starting rotation for today\u2019s push in Roto categories.",
